<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barotseland Agreement 1964</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Barotseland Agreement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Barotseland Agreement 1964 was signed in May 1964 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenneth-kaunda">Kenneth Kaunda</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwanawina-iii">Litunga Mwanawina III</a> and the British government. It made Barotseland part of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> while promising the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> kingdom its own institutions and a degree of self-government. The Zambian government abrogated it in 1969, and its status remains disputed by Lozi leaders.</p></div>
